The monitoring directory is for observability and performance monitoring of the Docker stack.

It contains two main parts:

- monitoring/prometheus/
  - Holds Prometheus configuration, especially prometheus.yml.
  - Prometheus collects metrics from services such as:
    - the backend API
    - cAdvisor (container metrics)
    - MySQL exporter
    - itself

- monitoring/grafana/
  - Holds Grafana configuration and dashboard provisioning.
  - prometheus.yml connects Grafana to Prometheus as a data source.
  - dashboard.yml tells Grafana to load dashboards automatically.
  - The dashboards themselves are under dashboards.

In simple terms:
- Prometheus collects metrics
- Grafana visualizes them in dashboards

So this directory is what makes your stack “monitorable” and gives you a dashboard view of health and performance.
